From: Yoshisato Yanagisawa <yyanagisawa@chromium.org>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 10:52:37 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 23/48] Extensions: Management: Restrict enabling of
 non-allowlisted extensions

Extensions disabled due to `DISABLE_NOT_ALLOWLISTED` require explicit
user re-enablement via `chrome://extensions`. Previously,
`ManagementSetEnabledFunction` allowed calling extensions with
management permission to programmatically re-enable these extensions,
which unintentionally transitioned them to a user-acknowledged state
and cleared allowlist enforcement.

This change adds a check in `ManagementSetEnabledFunction` to prevent
calling extensions from enabling target extensions disabled with
`disable_reason::DISABLE_NOT_ALLOWLISTED`. Re-enabling remains allowed
for non-extension contexts such as the management WebUI.

Fixed: 514542988
Change-Id: Icdafb0ab6de467ea8e95817cadb46764f96b31bf
Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8421639
Reviewed-by: Eva Su <evasu@chromium.org>
Commit-Queue: Solomon Kinard <solomonkinard@chromium.org>
